      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "CB1R has no signal peptide; its N-terminus (residues 1\u2013116) is entirely extracellular per the topology landmarks. A tag prepended before Met1 is therefore on the extracellular face. L4 explicitly reports SSF-CB1R surface-labeled with a non-cell-permeant antibody, and L8 reports that the same SSF-tagged construct (combined with the F180 modification) shows normal internalization kinetics, confirming surface display and function. The position is topology-derived because no residue number is stated for the N-terminal junction, but only one extracellular terminus exists here. SSF-CB1R construct expressed in neurons; non-cell-permeant Alexa647-M1-FLAG antibody applied before experiment to label surface receptor; sub-cellular localization analysis confirmed plasma-membrane display of the N-terminally tagged full-length receptor.",
